 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls**
 *   **Truncation:** The GauPF relies on a truncation function $\lambda$ to handle points far from any Gaussian center; failure to truncate can lead to numerical instability or incorrect probability mapping [S1].
-*   **Discretization:** While the representation is continuous, the final output requires extracting discrete Gaussians. The source notes an "octree-guided sampling and optimization" algorithm for this extraction, implying that naive sampling from the continuous functions may not yield optimal discrete primitives without this post-processing step [S1].
